  "solution": {
    "text": "A] The molecular orbital energy configuration of <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> is<br /><math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br />In the MO of <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> there is no unpaired electron hence it is diamagnetic<br />B] Bond order of <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> is 3 and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is 2 therefore bond length of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is greater than <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math><br />C] The molecular orbital energy configuration of <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> is<br /><math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br />Bond order of <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn></math><br />The molecular orbital energy configuration of <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi></msubsup></math><br />Bond order of <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn></math><br />D] <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> has less energy as compare to two isolated He atoms"
  }
